WEBVTT

00:01.780 --> 00:05.450
<i>To my brother and sister-in-law traveling in Hokkaido,</i>

00:05.520 --> 00:06.980
<i>how are you?</i>

00:07.090 --> 00:09.730
<i>I'm fine... probably.</i>

00:10.020 --> 00:14.020
<i>I'd love it if you brought back salted salmon or something as a souvenir.</i>

00:14.080 --> 00:15.700
<i>No marimo, please.</i>

00:15.700 --> 00:18.060
<i>I sprained my foot recently.</i>

00:18.160 --> 00:21.200
<i>All the blame can be traced back to Usami Akihiko.</i>

00:21.520 --> 00:23.230
Mi-sa-ki~

00:25.230 --> 00:27.040
What's this? That hurt you know?

00:28.040 --> 00:30.760
Sorry! It was you Sumi-senpai!

00:31.270 --> 00:33.360
<i>I thought it was stupid Usagi...</i>

00:35.310 --> 00:36.470
How's your foot?

00:36.880 --> 00:39.300
Oh, it's alright now.

00:39.860 --> 00:42.740
But senpai, I'm really sorry.

00:43.150 --> 00:45.920
I couldn't help out with the festival preparations.

00:46.350 --> 00:48.320
That's okay. Don't worry.

00:49.460 --> 00:52.540
But still, I really did want to help out.

00:53.080 --> 00:56.210
<i>In the first place, speaking of the reason for my sprain...</i>

00:56.220 --> 00:59.520
Misaki-kun's Path to Sprainage

00:56.750 --> 00:59.520
Misaki-kun's Path to Sprainage- Start!!

01:00.080 --> 01:01.490
I meet the elder Usagi.

01:01.200 --> 01:05.980
ani

01:02.420 --> 01:06.080
Try to fend off his strawberry offensive by explaining, but he didn't listen.

01:06.410 --> 01:09.710
"I want to have a proper chat", he says and summons me to his house.

01:09.870 --> 01:11.440
His house is the Usagi family home.

01:11.740 --> 01:12.930
I was a bit curious.

01:13.930 --> 01:15.670
And so, off we go!

01:16.560 --> 01:19.040
His house was practically a theme park!

01:19.980 --> 01:22.210
Usagi-ani locks me in a room.

01:22.700 --> 01:24.100
Get me out of here!

01:23.060 --> 01:23.630
Pinch!

01:24.460 --> 01:26.490
So I use some nearby sheets as a makeshift rope.

01:26.640 --> 01:28.120
A sheet tears.

01:27.040 --> 01:28.060
Crash

01:28.430 --> 01:32.320
<b>Misaki-kun falls down</b>

01:28.560 --> 01:32.490
Misaki-kun falls down- GOOOAAAL!!

01:33.680 --> 01:36.710
If you want to help that much, how about at the festival itself?

01:36.760 --> 01:38.710
Eh? Really!?

01:39.120 --> 01:41.440
It'll just be simple stuff though, like pulling in customers.

01:41.600 --> 01:43.280
I'll do it! I'll go for it!!

01:43.330 --> 01:47.120
Old town mystery, steamy onsen and delicious food, murder in a mixed-sex bath,

01:47.280 --> 01:51.790
a casual journey of exploration and discovery, the maid who saw it all...!!

01:50.330 --> 01:53.020
But it's just a haunted house.

01:53.060 --> 01:58.010
From within the lie comes the truth

01:58.340 --> 02:03.590
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:58.340 --> 02:03.590
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:01.140 --> 02:14.410
Junjou Romantica 2

02:03.590 --> 02:07.060
ima futari no story

02:03.590 --> 02:07.060
Now, our story...

02:08.350 --> 02:15.840
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

02:08.350 --> 02:15.840
Our future is going to shine on.

02:19.280 --> 02:24.570
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

02:19.280 --> 02:24.570
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

02:25.040 --> 02:29.400
okubyou ni naru bakari

02:25.040 --> 02:29.400
and always lose my nerve.

02:29.400 --> 02:35.000
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

02:29.400 --> 02:35.000
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

02:35.000 --> 02:38.630
kimi to aeru nara

02:35.000 --> 02:38.630
if it means I can see you.

02:40.660 --> 02:45.640
ame ni utarete furueru koe

02:40.660 --> 02:45.640
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

02:45.970 --> 02:51.240
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

02:45.970 --> 02:51.240
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

02:51.920 --> 02:54.720
boku wa yuku yo

02:51.920 --> 02:54.720
I'll go,

02:54.720 --> 03:01.470
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

02:54.720 --> 03:01.470
Until the day when I can see you.

03:02.290 --> 03:07.480
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

03:02.290 --> 03:07.480
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

03:07.480 --> 03:11.190
ima futari no story

03:07.480 --> 03:11.190
Now, our story

03:11.350 --> 03:13.000
ugokidashita

03:11.350 --> 03:13.000
has started.

03:13.000 --> 03:17.990
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

03:13.000 --> 03:17.990
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

03:17.990 --> 03:25.180
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

03:17.990 --> 03:25.180
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

03:31.190 --> 03:31.910
What?

03:32.150 --> 03:34.470
Sorry, the front gate's too dangerous.

03:34.720 --> 03:38.570
What's the big deal? Usami-san's just here to pick you up again, right?

03:39.040 --> 03:41.730
That's why! It's seriously embarrassing!

03:42.380 --> 03:47.770
<i>Because I got injured, Usagi-san started restricting me more than ever before.</i>

03:48.270 --> 03:51.320
<i>He hardly lets me do anything now...</i>

03:52.280 --> 03:55.440
That's nice. Feels like you're really being loved.

03:55.620 --> 03:56.500
Huh!?

03:56.770 --> 03:57.500
Love

04:01.210 --> 04:06.240
I thought love was supposed to be more of an enchantingly wonderful pink color...

04:06.330 --> 04:07.390
Ehhh...?

04:08.070 --> 04:11.220
Dark, black love. I really like that.

04:11.660 --> 04:12.900
Huh...

04:19.220 --> 04:22.240
EHH!!? Why are you here!!?

04:22.590 --> 04:26.130
Why does your brain work in such predictably simplistic ways?

04:27.130 --> 04:30.300
Today, I am walking home with senpai, so go home ahead of me.

04:30.550 --> 04:32.880
Hello, Usami-sensei.

04:33.270 --> 04:35.360
Do that after your wounds are healed.

04:35.550 --> 04:37.310
They've already healed!

04:37.460 --> 04:39.120
Speaking of which, whose fault was it-

04:43.640 --> 04:45.690
Stupid! Let me out! Let me out!

04:44.520 --> 04:48.320
I'm sure you're aware of our school festival this weekend.

04:48.580 --> 04:52.850
The person whose going to help out our circle is Misaki.

04:53.680 --> 04:57.950
So I'm afraid he'll be my captive for that one day, but...

04:58.490 --> 04:59.710
you won't might, right?

05:01.610 --> 05:02.310
That's a no.

05:08.200 --> 05:09.950
What was that!?

05:10.090 --> 05:14.970
Are you that determined to destroy my fun and exciting college life?

05:15.600 --> 05:17.790
Are you still hanging out with that kid?

05:18.180 --> 05:19.940
I thought I told you not to!

05:21.470 --> 05:24.650
Listen, I think I said this before,

05:25.100 --> 05:30.110
I don't think it's a good idea to jump to conclusions about people you don't even know.

05:30.490 --> 05:32.080
Who's the one who doesn't know?

05:32.080 --> 05:33.550
It's you!

05:33.740 --> 05:35.840
Senpai really is a good person.

05:36.080 --> 05:37.960
He teaches me many things.

05:42.840 --> 05:45.930
He's trying to go after you! Can't you understand that?

05:46.430 --> 05:47.150
Huh?

05:47.830 --> 05:48.720
After me?

05:49.410 --> 05:50.520
Senpai is?

05:52.600 --> 05:55.120
Are you stupid? There's no way that's possible.

05:55.170 --> 05:56.400
You're the idiot!

05:56.500 --> 05:58.600
Shut up! Let go of me!

05:58.680 --> 06:00.610
You're immediately swept away by the flow.

06:00.700 --> 06:02.160
That's not true!

06:02.670 --> 06:05.090
And besides, I'm not an elementary school kid!

06:05.230 --> 06:07.930
Don't put so many restrictions on me just because of a sprain!

06:08.130 --> 06:10.290
Restrictions? That's just my love!

06:10.320 --> 06:11.790
What part of it is love?

06:12.010 --> 06:15.570
In any case, stop hanging around with him.

06:15.650 --> 06:17.760
Mind your own business!

06:20.030 --> 06:21.770
Cut it out!

06:22.420 --> 06:24.850
Don't club senpai with your kind!

06:27.120 --> 06:29.310
This time, let me make this clear,

06:29.470 --> 06:34.160
who I hang out with or what I do, I have no obligation of telling any of it to you.

06:34.310 --> 06:37.670
And you have no right to say anything about it too!

06:40.750 --> 06:41.740
<i>What?</i>

06:42.440 --> 06:45.960
<i>Usually, he would have immediately argued back already</i>

06:47.200 --> 06:50.490
<i>It's kind of awkward? Or so I think.</i>

06:52.050 --> 06:56.270
T-That said, I think I'll go shopping for dinner or something...

06:56.880 --> 06:59.990
I... love you.

07:01.290 --> 07:02.290
That's why...

07:03.710 --> 07:04.500
That's why...

07:05.440 --> 07:08.790
T-That's right! Let's have kimchi stew for dinner!

07:08.910 --> 07:14.250
You know, if you fry up the kimchi with some oil before putting it in the pot, it tastes super delicious!

07:14.400 --> 07:15.890
So then, I'm going~

07:22.710 --> 07:28.320
Uhh, sheesh... It's these surprise moves he suddenly pulls out of nowhere that really freak me out.

07:29.470 --> 07:32.010
Sumi-senpai is just a friend!

07:32.080 --> 07:36.810
And besides, if he thinks I'd just blindly follow anybody, then he's mistak-

07:40.990 --> 07:43.650
Oh, no, but you see, that was...

07:46.010 --> 07:46.640
Hello?

07:47.090 --> 07:47.860
It's me.

07:48.200 --> 07:49.770
<i>Usagi-ani!!!</i>

07:50.130 --> 07:51.440
<i>Wait a minute!</i>

07:52.090 --> 07:54.190
<i>Why does he know my cell number?</i>

07:55.260 --> 07:56.960
How's your foot injury?

07:57.280 --> 08:00.230
Eh...Ah... It's alright now.

08:00.630 --> 08:02.760
Actually, why do you know my number?

08:02.850 --> 08:05.420
I wanted to talk to you once more.

08:05.700 --> 08:07.230
I love you.

08:07.760 --> 08:08.330
That's why...

08:08.790 --> 08:11.070
I'm sorry. It's impossible!

08:14.220 --> 08:15.220
<i>See! Look!</i>

08:15.680 --> 08:19.550
<i>When required, I too can properly turn someone down, on my own.</i>

08:20.420 --> 08:22.260
<i>I don't get swept away.</i>

08:22.870 --> 08:25.360
<i>Sumi-senpai is my senior and friend.</i>

08:26.690 --> 08:28.700
<i>Usagi-ani, I don't understand about him, but</i>

08:29.590 --> 08:31.170
<i>he's Usagi-san's elder brother...</i>

08:31.920 --> 08:33.180
<i>And Usagi-san is...</i>

08:36.720 --> 08:39.960
<i>Usagi-san is... Usagi-san obviously.</i>

08:41.140 --> 08:44.960
54th Mitsuhashi University Festival

08:47.140 --> 08:48.630
The Hall of Hell

08:48.650 --> 08:51.630
Haunted House

08:49.400 --> 08:50.990
Senpai!

08:51.890 --> 08:53.520
Oh, Misaki!

08:54.170 --> 08:56.190
This stuff really suits you.

08:56.320 --> 08:58.100
Really? Heh.

08:58.520 --> 09:00.600
Especially the sagging around your feet.

09:01.030 --> 09:02.040
"Loose bear."

09:02.550 --> 09:06.690
Well, sorry! For having short feet!

09:06.850 --> 09:09.920
Oops! Don't yell. You'll suffocate.

09:12.930 --> 09:17.560
But though this is a haunted house, why are we luring in customers with animal suits?

09:17.280 --> 09:28.290
Onsen Research Group's
54th Haunted House

09:17.760 --> 09:19.790
Well, in our case...

09:20.850 --> 09:24.780
For generations, we've been known as the makers of Japan's most terrifying haunted house.

09:25.000 --> 09:26.980
So we've got to pull them with something cute.

09:30.440 --> 09:33.470
What in the world have you put inside there?

09:33.830 --> 09:35.510
Isn't Usami-san coming today?

09:35.950 --> 09:39.330
Oh, ummm, probably. He seemed to be caught up in some work.

09:40.800 --> 09:44.700
<i>Ever since that day, Usagi-san and I haven't really spoken to each other.</i>

09:45.210 --> 09:47.680
<i>He always drops me off and picks me up like always, but...</i>

09:49.420 --> 09:51.810
<i>Did I... say something harsh?</i>

09:53.120 --> 09:53.850
Misaki!

09:54.170 --> 09:54.870
Customers.

09:54.900 --> 09:56.130
Yup, coming!

09:56.130 --> 09:57.600
Here, for you.

09:57.040 --> 09:57.820
Thank you.

09:57.850 --> 09:58.990
<i>Enough!</i>

09:59.200 --> 10:02.510
<i>For now, I'm going to enjoy the Festival.</i>

10:08.510 --> 10:10.320
Who's up for the next after-party?

10:10.370 --> 10:12.350
We are!!

10:11.550 --> 10:12.490
I'll pass.

10:12.660 --> 10:13.610
Why!?

10:15.000 --> 10:15.960
Bye then!

10:15.960 --> 10:18.290
How about you Misaki? You okay with the last train timing?

10:18.460 --> 10:21.090
Oh, is it this late already?

10:22.650 --> 10:24.730
Oh, excuse me for a bit.

10:26.840 --> 10:30.260
Uh, but I did leave you a note...

10:31.690 --> 10:33.380
I got it!

10:34.540 --> 10:36.840
You don't have to come. I'm hanging up.

10:37.510 --> 10:38.430
Was that Usami-san?

10:39.000 --> 10:40.000
Uh, yeah.

10:40.310 --> 10:44.900
Actually, I did inform him that I'd be home late since today was the festival.

10:45.410 --> 10:46.640
Look at this!

10:47.240 --> 10:49.150
There are 18 missed calls!

10:50.900 --> 10:52.960
It's good to see he's worried about you.

10:53.270 --> 10:54.780
It's not good.

10:54.960 --> 10:56.700
You're not very honest, are you?

10:58.200 --> 10:59.400
So, what should we do?

10:59.870 --> 11:01.280
Want to stay at my place tonight?

11:01.990 --> 11:03.340
Eh? Is that okay?

11:03.820 --> 11:05.820
My parents aren't home tonight.

11:06.320 --> 11:11.220
Oh... speaking of which, what do your parents do?

11:11.480 --> 11:12.540
Hmm...

11:12.670 --> 11:13.630
Novelists?

11:14.040 --> 11:15.080
Wha...!?

11:15.430 --> 11:17.420
Same as Usagi-san, right?

11:18.460 --> 11:22.870
Misaki, your phone's too noisy, so switch it to vibrating mode, okay?

11:26.730 --> 11:29.760
Misaki! Is this toothbrush okay?

11:34.210 --> 11:35.040
Oh, my.

11:36.680 --> 11:37.620
Hey~!

11:38.580 --> 11:40.750
If you sleep with your tummy showing, you're going to catch a cold.

11:45.530 --> 11:47.110
...bear...

12:00.140 --> 12:00.600
Yes?

12:02.140 --> 12:02.980
Who's this?

12:03.170 --> 12:05.120
It's Sumi, Usami-sensei.

12:05.700 --> 12:08.080
Misaki's sleeping quite peacefully right now,

12:08.940 --> 12:10.390
so he can't attend the phone.

12:11.000 --> 12:11.960
Where are you?

12:12.370 --> 12:13.380
At my house.

12:13.820 --> 12:18.040
Today, he worked really hard to help us out, so he seems really tired.

12:19.160 --> 12:20.920
You should have come too.

12:21.490 --> 12:23.680
Misaki looked really cute.

12:25.000 --> 12:26.450
I'm coming to get him right now.

12:27.340 --> 12:28.900
Could you tell me your address?

12:30.190 --> 12:32.340
Is that so? Then...

12:32.960 --> 12:37.530
...since it's you, you should be able to find out the address of the novelist, Sumi Ryuichiro.

12:38.710 --> 12:41.480
If you don't come for him quickly, then I don't know what will happen.

12:41.580 --> 12:43.840
Hey! What are you thinking!?

12:45.350 --> 12:46.130
Who knows...?

13:00.780 --> 13:02.890
Welcome, Usami-sensei.

13:03.580 --> 13:04.660
Where's Misaki?

13:05.590 --> 13:07.340
How about coming inside?

13:08.110 --> 13:10.260
My parents aren't home today.

13:11.580 --> 13:13.850
To think you're Sumi-sensei's son...

13:14.930 --> 13:17.350
The world is a pretty small place.

13:18.260 --> 13:19.480
Where's Misaki?

13:21.440 --> 13:22.770
I'll make some tea.

13:23.310 --> 13:24.780
Or would sake be better?

13:25.110 --> 13:28.070
No, I don't want either. We'll be going home soon.

13:28.870 --> 13:34.980
My father was on the selection committee that awarded you the best novelist award when you debuted,

13:35.800 --> 13:39.450
so I've been hearing all about you ever since I was a child.

13:39.970 --> 13:42.620
Thanks to that, I've read all of your books.

13:43.470 --> 13:44.670
And not just books,

13:45.240 --> 13:48.380
interviews, columns, talks, everything.

13:49.460 --> 13:51.900
No matter what it was, I didn't like a single one.

13:55.630 --> 13:58.330
In the first place, I don't like novelists at all.

13:59.810 --> 14:03.020
All the little pipe dream stories that you think up,

14:03.620 --> 14:06.400
are just being imposed on other people, is what I feel.

14:06.800 --> 14:09.110
"That's such a waste", is what I think.

14:13.130 --> 14:17.310
When I read your debut novel, I ended up crying.

14:18.100 --> 14:22.180
Not just that one novel, somehow every book you have ever written,

14:23.820 --> 14:27.360
for some reason, has ended up shattering my values.

14:28.300 --> 14:30.380
Don't you think that's aggravating?

14:31.300 --> 14:34.380
What gives you the right to do that?

14:35.640 --> 14:37.460
If you don't like them, don't read them.

14:37.840 --> 14:38.530
Don't like?

14:39.910 --> 14:42.520
I understand clearly that you hate me.

14:43.300 --> 14:44.250
Hate?

14:45.390 --> 14:47.200
Who said anything like that?

14:47.560 --> 14:48.530
I...

14:52.830 --> 14:54.860
...like you, actually.

15:12.700 --> 15:14.720
I fell asleep.

15:17.270 --> 15:19.900
Is <i>this</i> why you got close to Misaki?

15:20.520 --> 15:22.280
Yes, that's right.

15:22.930 --> 15:24.200
Enough with the jokes.

15:24.570 --> 15:25.280
Move.

15:25.620 --> 15:26.660
Joking?

15:26.900 --> 15:27.880
Usagi-san!?

15:28.850 --> 15:30.270
<i>Why is he here?</i>

15:32.740 --> 15:33.230
So?

15:34.170 --> 15:37.860
I understand well that you love Misaki.

15:38.220 --> 15:40.260
But for now, won't you let me hold you?

15:41.200 --> 15:43.480
You can fall in love with me afterwards.

15:44.850 --> 15:46.450
Eh!? What?

15:47.310 --> 15:48.810
What did he say just now?

15:49.510 --> 15:51.900
This kind of thing is your forte, right?

15:53.820 --> 15:56.180
After all, this is how it was with Misaki too, right?

16:03.940 --> 16:06.490
Oh? So it <i>was</i> like that, then.

16:07.120 --> 16:11.600
Well, given how Misaki reacts to you, it's rather obvious.

16:13.660 --> 16:15.680
So think as this being the same...

16:19.440 --> 16:20.660
That's wrong!!

16:22.350 --> 16:23.820
That... Whoa...!

16:24.990 --> 16:26.740
What the hell are you two doing!?

16:27.660 --> 16:28.830
Say, Misaki,

16:30.020 --> 16:31.580
could you give this person to me?

16:31.720 --> 16:32.350
What?

16:33.030 --> 16:38.210
You're always complaining about him and acting like you can't stand him.

16:39.170 --> 16:43.740
Honestly speaking, I think, I know him much better than you do.

16:44.200 --> 16:47.120
Uh... No... But...

16:47.940 --> 16:48.560
<i>What?</i>

16:49.220 --> 16:51.140
<i>What is senpai saying!?</i>

16:52.020 --> 16:54.980
You don't have to put up with someone you don't like, right?

16:55.770 --> 16:58.480
No... I don't really...

17:00.440 --> 17:03.760
<i>Hey, stupid Usagi! You say something too!</i>

17:04.320 --> 17:09.100
<i>Besides, I never really said anything about hating Usagi-san or anything.</i>

17:10.460 --> 17:12.600
I'll take him off of your hands.

17:13.040 --> 17:14.780
You can stay at your brother's home or something.

17:15.270 --> 17:18.100
<i>Usagi-san is... Usagi-san is...</i>

17:21.840 --> 17:23.280
That won't do!!

17:23.400 --> 17:26.280
I won't give him up to you or anyone else!

17:26.320 --> 17:28.340
Usagi-san belongs to me!!

17:41.590 --> 17:43.470
No... senpai... um...!

17:43.940 --> 17:45.060
Right now...!

17:46.870 --> 17:48.090
That's how it is.

17:50.060 --> 17:51.780
The one I love is Misaki.

17:53.940 --> 17:54.920
Not you.

17:55.730 --> 17:57.540
Um, senpai...!

17:57.700 --> 17:58.480
Let's go.

18:16.510 --> 18:18.760
And what the hell was that!?

18:19.230 --> 18:23.340
If you have time to be squawking about me, watch your damn self a little!

18:25.100 --> 18:27.380
What in the world were you doing?

18:27.480 --> 18:29.630
You're in way more danger than I am!

18:30.110 --> 18:31.520
Hey, are you listening!?

18:35.480 --> 18:38.150
W-What is it? Let go of me!

18:38.380 --> 18:40.500
I'm really angry, you know!

18:41.940 --> 18:42.790
I love you.

18:43.550 --> 18:47.010
S-So, you always use that trick to fudge the conversation.

18:47.080 --> 18:48.030
I love you!

18:48.960 --> 18:50.080
Shut up!

18:50.190 --> 18:51.620
I'm going to sleep.

18:55.560 --> 18:56.480
I love you.

18:57.450 --> 18:58.380
What is it?

18:59.180 --> 19:03.040
I, whether you like it or hate it, am absolutely never letting go of you.

19:03.110 --> 19:04.440
Usagi-san?

19:05.320 --> 19:09.330
If you run away, I'll probably go chasing after you and lock you up.

19:10.310 --> 19:12.420
Hey, hey! That'd be bad!

19:14.300 --> 19:15.400
I know.

19:16.560 --> 19:18.540
Usagi-san, what happened?

19:19.630 --> 19:20.840
You're acting strange.

19:21.400 --> 19:22.550
Misaki...

19:22.720 --> 19:24.640
Kiss me.

19:25.000 --> 19:28.190
<i>Eh? Wha? Eh? What's that!?</i>

19:28.600 --> 19:30.850
I-I-Impossible! I'll have to decline!

19:31.050 --> 19:32.770
That's too high-level for me!

19:32.820 --> 19:35.070
Anyway, let's turn on the lights.

19:35.200 --> 19:37.420
Darkness is not good in the lot of ways!

19:40.100 --> 19:42.220
W-Wai-... Usagi-san!

19:43.310 --> 19:44.620
What's with you?

19:44.680 --> 19:45.600
What's-...?

19:53.340 --> 19:54.750
St-Stop-!

19:55.550 --> 19:56.840
What's the matter with you?

19:57.500 --> 19:59.400
You're definitely acting strange today!

20:33.700 --> 20:36.020
After all, this is how it was with Misaki too, right?

20:38.760 --> 20:40.640
<i>I love you.</i>

20:42.310 --> 20:43.240
<i>That's why...</i>

21:05.800 --> 21:10.940
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:05.800 --> 21:10.940
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:11.070 --> 21:16.330
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:11.070 --> 21:16.330
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:16.680 --> 21:21.700
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:16.680 --> 21:21.700
You doubled all my happiness,

21:21.700 --> 21:28.390
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:21.700 --> 21:28.390
and halved all my sadness.

21:28.500 --> 21:33.500
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

21:28.500 --> 21:33.500
No matter what path I walk in the future,

21:33.900 --> 21:38.180
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

21:33.900 --> 21:38.180
will surely lead to you.

21:38.180 --> 21:40.940
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

21:38.180 --> 21:40.940
You're there up ahead of me,

21:40.940 --> 21:43.800
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

21:40.940 --> 21:43.800
I'm there ahead of you,

21:43.800 --> 21:49.070
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

21:43.800 --> 21:49.070
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

21:49.070 --> 21:54.970
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

21:49.070 --> 21:54.970
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

21:55.560 --> 22:00.040
mou doko he mo ikanaide

21:55.560 --> 22:00.040
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:00.040 --> 22:05.500
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:00.040 --> 22:05.500
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:05.500 --> 22:10.890
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:05.500 --> 22:10.890
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:10.890 --> 22:16.710
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:10.890 --> 22:16.710
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:17.100 --> 22:22.390
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:17.100 --> 22:22.390
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:26.980 --> 22:29.390
Oh, Misaki-kun, welcome back.

22:29.770 --> 22:31.240
Oh, hello.

22:31.820 --> 22:33.020
Were you alright?

22:33.340 --> 22:36.100
Huh? Oh... yeah...

22:36.790 --> 22:38.450
<i>Was that about Sumi-senpai?</i>

22:39.020 --> 22:41.500
<i>Usagi-san is back to his old self again.</i>

22:39.830 --> 22:42.740
Sensei, you're on a roll again today!

22:41.700 --> 22:43.170
<i>And speaking about senpai...</i>

22:45.020 --> 22:48.700
I have a printout of the pictures from yesterday.

22:49.260 --> 22:50.590
Let me know the numbers of the pictures you want.

22:51.040 --> 22:52.420
I'll email them to you.

22:53.060 --> 22:53.900
Okay.

22:55.300 --> 22:57.060
<i>He isn't a bad person, isn't he?</i>

22:57.470 --> 23:01.020
<i>Though, it was his fault that I ended up blurting out some weird stuff.</i>

23:01.540 --> 23:04.170
<i>but, well, given the situation, that was only natural...</i>

23:04.320 --> 23:09.180
Sensei, about that, I do think the uke here should a bit more emotionally...

23:09.240 --> 23:09.810
<i>Huh?</i>

23:10.080 --> 23:12.480
In that case, what should the seme do, I wonder.

23:12.560 --> 23:17.140
Hmm, then, how about introducing a new character and making it a love triangle?

23:13.370 --> 23:15.100
<i>"Seme"? "Uke"?</i>

23:15.600 --> 23:17.730
<i>Is this another freaking BL brainstorm session?</i>

23:18.320 --> 23:18.750
<i>Ah!</i>

23:19.840 --> 23:20.900
<i>In that case...</i>

23:22.080 --> 23:23.550
<i>...Usagi-san was the uke!?</i>

23:24.550 --> 23:26.290
<i>Setting that truth aside,</i>

23:26.560 --> 23:30.720
<i>still oblivious to the mountain of tempestous trouble that lay ahead,</i>

23:30.890 --> 23:34.370
<i>it was Takahashi Misaki, in his 19th year in the autumn.</i>

23:57.000 --> 24:00.000
A picture is worth a thousand words
